A||||39||151 in. of love||fire......||||9||
Z||000000||151 in. of love||02-20-2001||02:11 AM||||(TAPS plays softly in the background)<P>Saturday night-<BR> I was getting ready to spend a few hours working on the Fiero. So I got a propane heater to keep me company and warm. <BR> I had just replaced the EGR on my newly rebuilt 2.5l 85 2m4 with 400 miles on the engine. I went to turn up the heat a little when....<BR>   WHOMPF!!!!!!!<BR> The valve had a leak and it shot a 6 foot flame up around me. I kicked the tank into the middle of the shop.<BR>  The tank stayed there burning without catching anything else on fire for about 10-15 min., while I called our local fire dept.<BR>  Then..BOOM!! the tank popped a leak and the flames subsided to about 2-3 foot. <BR>  When the fire dept. showed there was NO structure fire. THEY SPRAYED THE TANK WITH A STRAIGHT STREAM OF WATER! Well then, the tank shot across the shop and caught the wall on fire.....(the rest is history)....<P>IN REMEBERENCE OF....<BR>my 76 honda 550,<BR>81 Kawasaki 1000,<BR>77 honda 350,<BR>81 Suzuki 550,<BR>and worst of all -my restored Fiero...<BR>(all of which were not covered by insurance)<BR> Let us have a moment of silence.<BR>Not posting pics, it hurts too much....<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||overlord||02-20-2001||02:49 AM||||o geez.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||02-20-2001||02:59 AM||||Oh man.....................  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>At least you're ok.............<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000003||mrfiero||02-20-2001||04:18 AM||||Damn!  Does that make the fire department liable or are they immune?  It sounds like they attacked the fire the wrong way causing it to catch the garage on fire.  Also, if the fire dept was on scene how did it spread so fast?  Were they not prepared or ??  Just curious......thank goodness I have no experience with this.....I don't know what I'd do if I lost any of my Fieros to a fire! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Red Toyota MR2||02-20-2001||05:03 AM||||I do belive the fire dept is at fault here.  You should make a clame with your local goverment.  They should replace everything you lost, including the building, for not putting out the fire corecctly.  (you NEVER shoot water on hot metal!!! ESPECIALLY UNDER PRESSURE!!!!!)<P>Rick<BR>86 Toyota MR2<BR>84 Fiero 2M4 (Lime green krylon!)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric_PA||02-20-2001||06:35 AM||||Sorry to hear that.....<BR>They should not have used water on that tank. I would check into it.<BR>Eric||||reg||1
