Z||000036||GarethWright||02-22-2001||02:26 AM||||Yuk State Farm blech I have had problems with them before.  My last car was a (nearly) fully restored 1976 MG Midget that I had been working on since I owned it (tons of fun workin on that one, lol I about qualified for an amateur mechanics license)  Anyway, Insert Jeep Grand Cherokee at this point in the story, she had been drinking, rear ended me, and insured by, guess who? yup State Farm.  Midget Totaled, According to SF, Its an old car, and the brake lights were small (no idea what That had to do with anything) so we will give you $750 for it, No thanks.  I ended up getting $3660 for the Midget and giving $3450 for my current love, 87 GT.<P>I am Really sorry for your loss, I hope you get some compensation out of it.||||reg||1
Z||000037||ChadMan||02-22-2001||09:11 AM||||I KNEW IT!!!  I hate Scam Farm with a purple passion.  I can't believe they are running ads now with a theme of "Sure, our insurance is more expensive...but if you go with those cut-rate guys, what will you do without a State Farm agent to help you?"<P>I know what I'll do without a State Farm agent -- pay low premiums and get good, friendly service!<P>Again, 151 -- I couldn't be sorrier.  If I were God, I'd snap my fingers and give you back your Fiero and all your bikes.||||reg||8
